 "text": "Hello, how are things going? Of course. Does your roommate have a specific brand of gluten free bread they need to eat, or are they flexible about it? Ask your roommate. A flexible one is easier to plan around. In any case, there are basics like pasta, rice, and potatoes that are gluten free. Roughly speaking, white rice, couscous, and pasta without a gluey sauce are safe. Pasta with gluey sauce isn't. Same goes for bread and sandwiches. Then look for soy sauce that's gluten free. Many of the big brands are. Or use mild one that doesn't taste like soy. You' welcome. Your roommate is probably too. Not at all. There are plenty of gluten free toppings. Pick one that suits her taste, like sweet and salty prawns, or tofu in sweet sauce.",
